16. Interface vs Concrete Class Injection
    Interface Injection	Class Injection
    Flexible	Tight coupling
    Easy testing	Harder to mock
    AOP friendly	Limited

17. JVM / Memory Perspective
    Interface metadata in Method Area
    No object created for interface
    Reference variable can point to any implementation
    Ex: List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();


19. Common Tricky Interview Questions (4+ Years)

Q1. Can interface have constructor?
❌ No—no instance state.

Q2. Can interface extend multiple interfaces?
✅ Yes.

Q3. Can we have main method in interface?
✅ Yes (static).

Q4. Can interface have private methods?
✅ Yes (Java 9+)—for internal reuse.

Q5. Why variables are final in interface?
To keep contracts immutable.

Q6. Interface vs abstract class—when which?
Interface: contracts, multiple inheritance, Spring services
Abstract class: shared code/state
